---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import Link from '@/components/Link.astro'
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button'

---

<Layout class="max-w-7xl ">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="About" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', icon: 'lucide:info' }]} />
  <div class="flex py-1 text-6xl" style="margin-top: 10px;"
  >about me
  </div>
  <section>
    <div class="min-w-full">
      <div class="prose mb-8">
        <p class="mt-0 text-2xl">
          Hello! My name is Alaina.<br>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-0"></p>
          I am from Saint Paul, earned by bachelor's degree in Environmental Science in Denver, and am now back in the Twin Cities, based in Minneapolis.
          I worked at the Riley Purgatory Bluff Creek Watershed District in the southwest suburbs of the Twin Cities metro area for several years, 
          and I am currently in my first year of the University of Minnesota's MGIS program, during which I am working at the Polar Geospatial Center as a Geospatial Support Assistant.<br>
          <br>
          My interests include cartography, environmental GIS, sustainable urban areas, climate resilience, and GIS as a communication tool.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose mb-8">
        <p class="mt-0"></p>
          Between job positions, a MN Greencorps term, undergraduate studies, and graduate studies, 
          I have been fortunate to have been able to learn skills and gain knowledge for many different subject areas and 
          focuses.<br>
          <br>
          I first learned about GIS at the University of Denver with a GIS minor, continued to use it at
          the Riley Purgatory Bluff Creek Watershed District, and am continuing to learn more in the University
          of Minnesota's MGIS program. Additionally, I have done field work for my bachelor's degree and for MN Greencorps, graphic design for the Watershed District (and on my own time), 
          learned about environmental science and sustainability through it all, and am now learning more about coding and development
          at the University of Minnesota.<br>
          <br>
          To read more about specifics of the positions I have held and the experience I have gained, click the button below to view my resume. Thank you! 
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex py-2">
        <Link
            href="/public/static/Portoghese_Resume2025.pdf"
            class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'destructive' }) + ' group'}
        >
            Resume
        </Link>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
